**Design Rationale Summary:**

| Milestone | Rule Type | Justification |
|-----------|-----------|---------------|
| find rail | position_near_with_facing | max_distance=4 forces player to walk 3+ blocks forward |
| find red_stained_glass | position_near_with_facing | max_distance=5, workshop is ~12 blocks from spawn |
| mine red_stained_glass_pane | count_in_box_at_most | Block destruction check (no Silk Touch = no item drop) |
| find magenta_carpet | position_near_with_facing | max_distance=5, deep in mine at z=18 |
| craft oak_planks | inventory_has | Crafted item appears in inventory, min_count=1 for robustness |
| craft magenta_wool | inventory_has | Crafted item appears in inventory |
| build a table | count_in_box_at_least | Clean area with no pre-existing oak_planks, checks player-placed block |
| find gold_ore | position_near_with_facing | max_distance=5, deep in mine at z=18 |
| mine andesite_stairs | count_in_box_at_most | Block destruction check, generous box around stairs |
| eat pumpkin_pie | inventory_has | Proxy for obtaining pie from chest (navigational challenge); eating is trivial once obtained |

**Acknowledged Limitations:**
- `eat pumpkin_pie` checks possession rather than consumption. This is accepted as the best available proxy — the hard part is navigating to and looting the chest, which this verifies. The actual eating action (right-click while holding food) is trivial once the item is obtained.
- `build a table` relies on the player knowing the Minecraft convention of fence + plank = table. The task text mentions "build a table from fence posts and planks" as a hint.

